## CONFIRMED ROOT CAUSES

<<<<<<< HEAD
1. `public/css/home.css` (74.6 KiB, unminified, 63% unused) loaded with plain `<link>` tags in the document head — THREE references. Render-blocks ~1,530 ms on mobile. Never goes through the Next.js CSS pipeline.
2. LCP element is `div.hero__bg-image` (CSS `background-image` `/assets/images/hero-home-cover.webp`). Preload scanner cannot discover background images; LCP waits for stylesheet parse.
3. Tawk.to live chat boots on page load — 20 requests to embed.tawk.to / va.tawk.to + main-thread work. Desktop TBT (170ms) worse than mobile (70ms).
4. Both gtag.js and gtm.js load — 288.7 KiB total, 136.8 KiB never executed.
5. Five vanilla scripts in `public/js/` preloaded at high priority: `main.js`, `hero-lead-form.js`, `contact-booking-timezone.js`, `work-filters-fix.js`, `recordConsoleEvents.js`
6. `/assets/images/logo.webp` is 320×180 but renders at 78×44.
7. Homepage has ~2,027 DOM elements and ships ~14 KiB of legacy JS polyfills.

## WORKING RULES

- Make ONE change at a time. Never batch unrelated fixes.
- Performance-only refactor. Do not change visual appearance, layout, copy, or user-visible behaviour.
- Show the diff and wait for confirmation before writing files.
- After every change, list exactly which files were touched and why.
- If a change could affect CLS or cause layout shift, say so BEFORE making it.
- Do not add any dependency without explaining why first.
- Do not touch any file not asked about.
- If unsure whether something is safe, stop and ask instead of guessing.
- If any design risk appears on any page, tell the user in the menu first — the site is live.
